  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;THE LOST PRINCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BOOK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Lost Prince is a novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett, first published in 1915, about Marco Loristan, his father, and a street urchin named 'The Rat'."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRANCES HODGSON BURNETT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Frances Hodgson Burnett is a British-American author who wrote 'The Lost Prince', a novel about Marco Loristan and his father's efforts to overthrow a Samavian dictatorship."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARCO LORISTAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marco Loristan is the protagonist of 'The Lost Prince', a young man who forms a friendship with a street urchin named 'The Rat' and whose father is a Samavian patriot."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEFAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stefan is Marco's father and a Samavian patriot working to overthrow the cruel dictatorship in the kingdom of Samavia."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAMAVIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Samavia is a fictional kingdom where the story of 'The Lost Prince' takes place, ruled by a cruel dictatorship and where Marco's father is working to restore the rightful king."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE RAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Rat is a street urchin and friend of Marco Loristan in 'The Lost Prince', known for his military-like shouting and his role in a secret club."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONDON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"London is a city where Marco and his father seek refuge and where Marco forms a friendship with 'The Rat'."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRINCE IVAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prince Ivan is a character mentioned in a conversation with Marco, possibly another Samavian prince or nobleman."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHNNIE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Johnnie is a character mentioned in the last part of the text, likely a child who witnesses a comet and is present at the King's funeral."&lt;SEP&gt;"Johnnie is a character who experiences a serious epileptic fit at Buckingham Palace and is sent to Sandringham for care."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUEEN MARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Queen Mary is a character who summons doctors to examine Johnnie and later sends him to Sandringham."&lt;SEP&gt;"Queen Mary is mentioned in the last part of the text, likely referring to the Queen of England who attends the King's funeral."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KAISER WILHELM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kaiser Wilhelm is a character mentioned as one of the heads of state attending the King's funeral."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kaiser Wilhelm is mentioned as one of the heads of state attending the King's funeral."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kaiser Wilhelm is mentioned in the last part of the text, likely referring to the German Emperor who attends the King's funeral."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUCKINGHAM PALACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Buckingham Palace is the location where Johnnie's parents are called to attend the King's deathbed and funeral."&lt;SEP&gt;"Buckingham Palace is the location where Johnnie's parents are called to during the King's deathbed scene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Buckingham Palace is the royal residence where Johnnie's parents are called to during the King's deathbed scene."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE LITTLE BOOK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BOOK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Little Book is a novel by Selden Edwards, providing background for 'The Lost Prince', about Wheeler Burden's story in fin de siècle Vienna."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SELDEN EDWARDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Selden Edwards is an American writer who wrote 'The Little Book' and 'The Lost Prince', a sequel to 'The Little Book'."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHEELER BURDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wheeler Burden is a character in 'The Little Book', whose story is set in fin de siècle Vienna and is the basis for 'The Lost Prince' narrative."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELEANOR BURDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eleanor Burden is a character who tragically lost her first great love in fin de siècle Vienna and later settles into Boston society."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eleanor Burden is the protagonist of 'The Lost Prince', an 1890s Boston socialite who has resigned herself to marrying a man she should be with rather than the man she loves."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOSTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Boston is the city where Eleanor Burden settles into her expected place in society."&lt;SEP&gt;"Boston is the setting for Eleanor Burden's life in 'The Lost Prince', where she settles into her expected place in society and marries a suitable husband."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIENNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vienna is the setting for Wheeler Burden's story in 'The Little Book', where he tragically loses the first great love of his life."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIN DE SIÈCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fin de siècle refers to the late 19th century, a period in which 'The Little Book' and 'The Lost Prince' are set."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD WAR I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"World War I is an event mentioned in 'The Lost Prince', occurring during the time period of the story."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EUROPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Europe is the setting for the events in 'The Lost Prince', where various heads of state attend the King's funeral."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The King is a character mentioned in the last part of the text, likely referring to the monarch of a European country who is dying and whose funeral is attended by many heads of state."&lt;SEP&gt;"The King is a character who is on his deathbed at Buckingham Palace, attended by heads of state."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEADS OF STATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heads of State refer to the leaders of various European countries who attend the King's funeral."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHNNIE'S PARENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Johnnie's parents are called to Buckingham Palace to be by the King's deathbed, indicating their close relationship to the royal family."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPILEPTIC FIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An epileptic fit is a medical condition experienced by Johnnie during the King's funeral, leading to a serious health episode."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A comet is mentioned as an event that prompts Johnnie's parents to be called to Buckingham Palace."&lt;SEP&gt;"A comet is mentioned in the last part of the text, likely seen by Johnnie and his parents before the King's deathbed scene."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOOKLIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Booklist is a literary review that provides opinions on books, such as the pleasure of reading them."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIN DE SIÈCLE VIENNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fin de siècle Vienna is a historical location where Eleanor Burden tragically lost her first great love."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOSTON SOCIETY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Boston society is the social environment where Eleanor Burden settles into her expected place after returning from Vienna."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LALLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lalla is a character who volunteers to look after Johnnie to prevent him from being sent to an institution."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SANDRINGHAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sandringham is the location where Johnnie is sent to be cared for and isolated from others."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHARLOTTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Charlotte is a character pursued by Johnnie, who is a terrified bird flying away into a building."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRINCE GEORGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prince George is a character who witnesses the brinkmanship between the Allies and the Central Powers during diplomatic meetings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prince George witnesses the brinkmanship between the Allies and the Central Powers during diplomatic meetings."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARCHDUKE FRANZ FERDINAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Archduke Franz Ferdinand is a significant historical figure whose assassination led to the brinkmanship between the Allies and the Central Powers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Archduke Franz Ferdinand is implied to be a significant figure whose assassination led to the brinkmanship between the Allies and the Central Powers."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRINCE OF PERSIA : THE LOST CROWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prince of Persia : The Lost Crown is a title mentioned, possibly referring to a book or media product."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf</data>
    </node>
